# KDE Global Menu @VERSION@

Production release of the native KDE Plasma 6 Global Menu applet with desktop fallback.

## Highlights

- complete issue #14 fallback menu rework across File, Edit, View, Go, Tools, Settings, and Help;
- native-style Create New submenu with safe folder, file, URL, filesystem-link, and application-link creation;
- Plasma lock, logout, shell restart, desktop peek/restore, Overview, and Activities actions;
- common locations owned exclusively by Go, with no File/Go duplication;
- optional launchers disabled when their program is not installed;
- expanded hierarchy, dispatch, availability, confirmation, and path-safety regression tests.

## Final release gate

The release is published only after all required jobs pass:

- static repository, metadata, SPDX and QML validation;
- Release build and complete CTest suite;
- ASan + UBSan test suite;
- repeated D-Bus fallback → application menu → fallback stress tests;
- Debian testing packages on amd64 and arm64, installed, smoke-tested and uninstalled;
- Fedora 43 RPM packages on x86_64 and aarch64, installed, smoke-tested and uninstalled;
- Arch Linux x86_64 package built with `makepkg`, installed, smoke-tested and uninstalled;
- native Plasma plugin discovery with `QT_PLUGIN_PATH` unset;
- package dependency audits and SHA-256 checksums.

## Installation

Use the package matching your distribution and CPU architecture. Official Arch Linux is x86_64; Debian and Fedora assets are provided for both x86_64/amd64 and ARM64/aarch64.

See the repository `README.md` and `docs/INSTALL.md` for installation and upgrade instructions.
